{
  "description": "Client protection per route (FR-16), run like gate.json against the same fake upstream. `apiKey`: the caller's header is compared in constant time with a sealed secret. `jwt`: `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` signed by one of the listed public keys (TEST ONLY keys; EdDSA, ES256, RS256 — the algorithm comes from the key with the token's `kid`, a token whose `alg` differs is refused), with `iss` and `aud` equal to the route's (`aud` may be a list), `exp` required and `nbf` respected, with 60 s leeway. `turnstile`: the token from the header is checked at `verifyUrl` with a POST form `secret=<secret>&response=<token>`; the fake upstream's /turnstile answers {\"success\": true} only for the response `TEST-ONLY-turnstile-pass` and one of the runner's secrets. `honeypot`: a JSON body whose field is present and not \"\" or null is refused. Every failed check answers 401 client_unauthorized and forwards nothing; the API key, JWT and honeypot cost no upstream call, a Turnstile check one. Failed `apiKey` attempts (a wrong, missing or malformed key) are counted per client (REMOTE_ADDR, SEC-26): after 5 within 300 s every further request of that client to a route with an API key answers 429 rate_limited with Retry-After before the key is compared, even with the right key (T-71); the failed requests also count against the policy's limits. Cases run in order: three failures happen earlier in this file, the fourth and fifth are below.",
  "config": {
    "version": 1,
    "upstreams": {
      "fake": {
        "origin": "https://upstream.test:{port}",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "secret": "api-token"
        },
        "timeoutMs": 5000
      }
    },
    "routes": {
      "key": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/key",
        "upstream": "fake",
        "upstreamPath": "/echo",
        "maxBodyBytes": 0,
        "contentTypes": ["application/json"],
        "responseContentTypes": ["application/json"],
        "enabled": true,
        "origins": [],
        "rateLimit": null,
        "client": {
          "apiKey": {
            "header": "X-Api-Key",
            "secret": "client-key"
          }
        }
      },
      "jwt": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/jwt",
        "upstream": "fake",
        "upstreamPath": "/echo",
        "maxBodyBytes": 0,
        "contentTypes": ["application/json"],
        "responseContentTypes": ["application/json"],
        "enabled": true,
        "origins": [],
        "rateLimit": null,
        "client": {
          "jwt": {
            "issuer": "https://issuer.test",
            "audience": "moat-test",
            "keys": [
              {
                "kid": "test-ed",
                "alg": "EdDSA",
